cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GRAAFE in your research, please cite the paper below."
title: "GRAAFE: GRaph Anomaly Anticipation Framework for Exascale HPC systems"
abstract: >-
  GRAAFE is a graph neural network (GNN) framework for anticipating compute-node
  anomalies in exascale-class high-performance computing (HPC) systems. It trains
  a GNN on historical telemetry from the CINECA Marconi100 supercomputer to predict
  the probability of node anomalies within a future time window, and deploys the
  trained model online through a Kubernetes/Kubeflow MLOps pipeline connected to the
  ExaMon monitoring system.
